// Ch14 side errand (optional, B01, before the vows). Saltwrights may not approach the dais, so a hull-captain asks Toma,
// an Order man, to carry the flotilla's gift (a carved oar-pin) to the vow table. He does. It is still on the table
// when the trap springs; nobody comments then. Sets ch14_carried_the_gift.
title: ch14_side_the_oar_pin
location: ch14/lacquer_court
---
<<if $ch14_carried_the_gift>>
    Hull_captain as "Hull-captain" [soft_smile]: It's on the table. I saw. Thank you. #line:ch14_pin_001
<<else>>
    Hull_captain as "Hull-captain" [neutral]: You're Order. Stillguard, once. We can't go up to the dais. Would you carry this for us? #line:ch14_pin_002 #long
    Toma [neutral]: What is it? #line:ch14_pin_003
    Hull_captain as "Hull-captain" [neutral]: An oar-pin. Every hull in Hollowmere put a cut in it. It's to say: you're crew now. #line:ch14_pin_004
    Toma [neutral]: I will carry it. #line:ch14_pin_005
    <<set $ch14_carried_the_gift = true>>
<<endif>>
===
